---
import AdeGuide from '../../../components/ade/AdeGuide.astro';
import { course, law, CLAIM } from '../../../data/ade-eligibility';

const faqs = [
  { q: 'What is an ADE-1317 certificate?', a: `The Texas adult driver education certificate of completion. A licensed provider issues it after you pass the six-hour course, and it is the document DPS wants from you if you are ${law.requiredBand} and applying for a first Texas driver license.` },
  { q: 'How long does it take to get the certificate?', a: `Texas gives a provider up to ${course.certificateDays} working days after the course completion date to issue it. Ours is issued as soon as you pass, but the rule is the rule and a provider quoting ${course.certificateDays} working days is not doing anything wrong.` },
  { q: 'Does the ADE-1317 expire?', a: 'The certificate itself does not carry a short expiry the way the Impact Texas Drivers certificate does. The one with a 90-day clock is ITAD, and people confuse the two constantly.' },
  { q: 'What do I do with the certificate?', a: `Bring it to your DPS appointment with your other documents. It is the proof that you completed driver education, and it is what lets a licensed instructor confirm the highway sign and traffic law portions on your behalf.` },
  { q: 'What if I lose it?', a: 'Ask the provider that issued it for a replacement. Providers are required to keep student records, so a certificate can be reissued.' },
  { q: 'Is ADE-1317 the same as DE-964?', a: 'No. DE-964 is the minor driver education certificate, for the 32-hour teen course. ADE-1317 is the adult six-hour equivalent. DPS accepts either for third-party skills testing at 18 to 24, but they are not interchangeable documents.' },
];
---
<AdeGuide
  title="The ADE-1317 Certificate: What It Is and How You Get It | Road Ready Safety"
  description="The Texas adult driver education certificate — who needs one, the 15-working-day issuance rule, what to do with it, and why it is not the certificate with the 90-day clock."
  url="/adult-drivers-ed/texas/ade-1317-certificate"
  eyebrow="The course"
  h1="The ADE-1317 certificate"
  lede="This is the piece of paper the whole six hours exists to produce. It is also routinely confused with a different certificate that expires in 90 days, which is an expensive mistake to make."
  faqs={faqs}
  sources={[
    { label: '16 TAC §84.503(h), the 15-working-day issuance rule' },
    { label: 'Tex. Transp. Code §521.1601 and §521.167', href: 'https://statutes.capitol.texas.gov/Docs/TN/htm/TN.521.htm' },
    { label: 'Texas DPS, Third Party Skills Testing Program', href: 'https://www.dps.texas.gov/section/driver-license/third-party-skills-testing-program' },
  ]}
>
  <section class="flex flex-col gap-4">
    <h2 class="text-[22px] font-bold text-text leading-8" style="font-family:'Outfit',sans-serif;">What it is and who needs it</h2>
    <p class="text-[17px] text-text-body leading-[30px]">
      The ADE-1317 is the certificate of completion for the Texas adult six-hour driver education
      course. If you are {law.requiredBand} and applying for a first Texas driver license, §521.1601
      means DPS cannot issue the license without one. If you are 25 or older it is optional, and some
      people take the course anyway because it {CLAIM}.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="flex flex-col gap-4">
    <h2 class="text-[22px] font-bold text-text leading-8" style="font-family:'Outfit',sans-serif;">The two certificates people mix up</h2>
    <div class="overflow-x-auto">
      <table class="w-full border-collapse text-left">
        <thead>
          <tr class="border-b border-border">
            <th class="py-3 pr-4 text-sm font-semibold text-text">Certificate</th>
            <th class="py-3 pr-4 text-sm font-semibold text-text">Comes from</th>
            <th class="py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-text">Clock</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr class="border-b border-border align-top">
            <td class="py-4 pr-4 text-[15px] text-text-body leading-6"><strong>ADE-1317</strong><br />driver education completion</td>
            <td class="py-4 pr-4 text-[15px] text-text-body leading-6">Your course provider, after you pass</td>
            <td class="py-4 text-[15px] text-text-body leading-6">No short expiry</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-border align-top">
            <td class="py-4 pr-4 text-[15px] text-text-body leading-6"><strong>ITAD</strong><br />Impact Texas Adult Drivers</td>
            <td class="py-4 pr-4 text-[15px] text-text-body leading-6">DPS, free, after a one-hour video</td>
            <td class="py-4 text-[15px] font-semibold text-text leading-6">Valid 90 days</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="text-[17px] text-text-body leading-[30px]">
      You need both to sit a driving skills test at 18 to 24. Only one of them expires, and it is not
      this one. The trap that follows from that is set out in{' '}
      <a class="underline hover:no-underline" href="/adult-drivers-ed/texas/impact-texas-adult-drivers">the 90-day certificate trap</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="flex flex-col gap-4">
    <h2 class="text-[22px] font-bold text-text leading-8" style="font-family:'Outfit',sans-serif;">The {course.certificateDays}-working-day rule</h2>
    <p class="text-[17px] text-text-body leading-[30px]">
      Texas gives a provider up to {course.certificateDays} working days after your completion date
      to issue the certificate. That is a ceiling, not a target, and a good provider issues it
      immediately &mdash; but it is worth knowing the rule before you book a DPS appointment for the
      day after you finish. If a provider quotes you the full {course.certificateDays} days, they are
      within the rules and you should plan accordingly.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="flex flex-col gap-4">
    <h2 class="text-[22px] font-bold text-text leading-8" style="font-family:'Outfit',sans-serif;">Read next</h2>
    <ul class="flex flex-col gap-3 pl-5 m-0 list-disc marker:text-text-subtle">
      <li class="text-[17px] text-text-body leading-[30px]"><a class="underline hover:no-underline" href="/adult-drivers-ed/texas/texas-driver-license-documents">Everything to bring to the appointment</a></li>
      <li class="text-[17px] text-text-body leading-[30px]"><a class="underline hover:no-underline" href="/adult-drivers-ed/texas/final-exam">The examination that produces it</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</AdeGuide>
